            <ArticleTitle>Heterotopic pregnancy in a young adult: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>265-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Heterotopic gestation, although fairly common with assisted reproductive techniques, is very rare in natural conception. Here we are reporting a case of heterotopic pregnancy in a 27-year-old woman who presented with sign and symptoms of acute abdomen from aborting tubal pregnancy with intrauterine gestation at 7 weeks of amenorrhea.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
